+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+
+======================
+BPF_MAP_TYPE_COUNT_MIN
+======================
+
+``BPF_MAP_TYPE_COUNT_MIN`` provides a count-min sketch: approximate
+counts for any number of keys in memory that is fixed when the map is
+created. The sketch is ``depth`` rows of ``width`` counters with one
+hash function per row. Adding a count to a key adds it to one counter in
+each row, and the estimate for a key is the smallest of its counters.
+
+An estimate is never below the key's true count. If ``N`` is the total
+of all counts added, the estimate exceeds the true count by more than
+``e * N / width`` with probability at most ``exp(-depth)``. To bound the
+error by ``epsilon * N`` with probability ``1 - delta``, choose
+``width = ceil(e / epsilon)`` and ``depth = ceil(ln(1 / delta))``
+(Cormode and Muthukrishnan, 2005).
+
+The map has no keys, only values, and must be created with a
+``key_size`` of 0. A value is the bytes of the key being counted followed
+by a ``__u64`` count, so ``value_size`` is the size of the key plus 8 and
+must be larger than 8. ``max_entries`` is the width. The lower 4 bits of
+``map_extra`` set the depth; 0 selects the default of 5 rows. The hash
+seed is random unless the map is created with ``BPF_F_ZERO_SEED``.
+
+The counters take ``8 * width * depth`` bytes. Elements cannot be
+deleted or iterated, and the map may be used as an inner map.
+
+Usage
+=====
+
+Kernel BPF
+----------
+
+bpf_map_push_elem()
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. code-block:: c
+
+   long bpf_map_push_elem(struct bpf_map *map, const void *value, u64 flags)
+
+Adds the count in ``value`` to the key in ``value``. ``flags`` must be
+``BPF_ANY``. Returns ``0`` on success, or a negative error.
+
+bpf_map_peek_elem()
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. code-block:: c
+
+   long bpf_map_peek_elem(struct bpf_map *map, void *value)
+
+Returns the estimate for the key in ``value``, a number of 0 or more.
+The count in ``value`` is ignored and not changed.
+
+Userspace
+---------
+
+``BPF_MAP_UPDATE_ELEM`` adds the count in ``value`` to its key, like
+push. ``BPF_MAP_LOOKUP_ELEM`` reads the key from ``value`` and writes the
+estimate into the count of ``value``. In both, ``key`` must be ``NULL``.
+
+Examples
+========
+
+.. code-block:: c
+
+    struct cms_value {
+            __u64 tid;
+            __u64 count;
+    };
+
+    struct {
+            __uint(type, BPF_MAP_TYPE_COUNT_MIN);
+            __type(value, struct cms_value);
+            __uint(max_entries, 2719);      /* epsilon = 0.001 */
+            __uint(map_extra, 5);           /* delta = 0.0067 */
+    } writes SEC(".maps");
+
+    SEC("fentry/vfs_write")
+    int BPF_PROG(count_writes)
+    {
+            struct cms_value v = {
+                    .tid = (__u32)bpf_get_current_pid_tgid(),
+                    .count = 1,
+            };
+
+            bpf_map_push_elem(&writes, &v, BPF_ANY);
+            return 0;
+    }
+
+From user space, the estimate for a thread is read with:
+
+.. code-block:: c
+
+    struct cms_value v = { .tid = tid };
+
+    err = bpf_map_lookup_elem(map_fd, NULL, &v);
+    /* v.count is the estimate */
